            <ArticleTitle>Diabetic Cranio-Cervico-Radiculoplexus Neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1189-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmrj.2015.05.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1934-1482(15)00231-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of a 53-year-old man with type 2 diabetes mellitus in whom cervical-radiculoplexus neuropathy developed, with concomitant cranial and phrenic nerve involvement, occurring as a stepwise, monophasic course. The patient had a presumed remote history of idiopathic cervical-radiculoplexus neuropathy.</AbstractText>
